config MP2_WDT_TIMEOUT_S
	int "Watchdog timeout sent with SET_TIMEOUT (seconds)"
	default 32
	range 6 131
	help
	  32 is the DK's timeout-sec, the one Linux uses. OP-TEE's early
	  interrupt comes 5 s before it and needs 1 s more, hence 6 at the
	  least; 131 is INIT's maximum with the LSI at 32 kHz.

config MP2_WDT_PET_S
	int "Seconds between two PETs"
	default 5
	range 1 60
	help
	  Must stay under the timeout less OP-TEE's 5 s (a build assert).

config MP2_WDT_REFRESH_S
	int "Seconds of petting, then no more"
	default 60
	range 1 600
	help
	  A whole number of PET periods. After it the image stops petting
	  and the IWDG resets the board about MP2_WDT_TIMEOUT_S later. The
	  layer's lifetime (CONFIG_YAKOGL_STM32MP2_LIFETIME_S, prj.conf) must
	  exceed REFRESH_S + TIMEOUT_S + 30 (a build assert).

source "Kconfig.zephyr"
